  "handoff": {
    "summary": "SUMMARY: Received b=1 replay establishes all three schedules hard-feasible. Two-pin: tap P1@0, tap P2@1, pull P1@7, pull P2@8; 4 actions/2 impacts, preference false. Clip: install C@0, remove C@7; 2 actions/0 impacts, preference true and archived. Sleeve: detach H@0, install V@1, insert S,V@2, withdraw S,V@7, remove V@8, assemble H@9; 6 actions/0 impacts, preference true. Sleeve changes intact H into free S used in V; J03/J06 supply every primitive. Insertion completes exactly boundary 3; retain 4 at ticks 3-6, remove V boundary 9, restore H boundary 10. H restoration is optional for hard release, so compare offered six-action restoration fairly against release-only five. Freeze required holding/release, operator, exclusivity, identities and capacities. b alone is available: at b=2 all satisfy preference; adjacent b=0 preserves clip/sleeve qualification. Pin threshold is 2. This is a preference shift with no hard-feasible mechanism appearing: preserve AC11 no-opening and known clip dominance. Q remains unmeasured; refuse assumed theta, undeclared relaxation, mechanical novelty caused by b or global originality. Supplied replay is finite-model evidence, not physical execution; other settings are projections. No fresh construction or equal-search-budget proof.",
